course: dictionary
lesson: 15268
title: Sidestroke: a calm way to swim
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sidestroke is a way of swimming. You lie on your side in the water, not on your front or your back. «Mia does the sidestroke so that her face stays out of the water.» The clue is that her face stays out, so sidestroke must be a way of swimming that keeps your head up.
explain: Your legs do a scissor kick, opening and closing like the blades of scissors. Your arms take turns under the water, one pulling while the other rests. «Tom can swim sidestroke for the whole length of the pool.» The clue is "for the whole length", so sidestroke is a stroke you can keep going for a long time.
explain: Lifesavers use sidestroke because it is calm and saves energy. They can keep their faces out of the water and pull a tired person along. «The lifesaver swam sidestroke and towed the boy to the side.» The words "towed" and "pull" show that sidestroke is useful for helping people.
fact: Sidestroke is a noun. It is the name of a swimming stroke.
fact: «Sidestroke» means a way of swimming while lying on your side, with a scissor kick and arms moving one after the other under the water.
fact: Two useful phrases are «swim sidestroke» and «do the sidestroke».
fact: Lifesavers use sidestroke because it keeps the face out of the water and saves energy.
fact: You can also say «sidestroke» in general, as in «I love sidestroke», because it is uncountable.
exercise: «Sam can swim sidestroke, lying on his side.» What is sidestroke? | A way of running very fast | A game played on the sand | *A way of swimming while lying on your side | A jump from the high diving board
exercise: Why is sidestroke useful to a lifesaver? | *It keeps the face out of the water and saves energy | It lets them swim fast with no arms at all | It stops them needing to breathe | It makes them sink quickly so they can rest | It keeps the face out of the water so they can pull someone along
exercise: «Sam does the sidestroke with a scissor kick.» Find and copy one word that describes the kick. | *scissor | with | sidestroke | does
test: «Lena swam sidestroke across the pool without stopping.» What does this tell you about sidestroke? | *It is a stroke you can keep swimming for a long way | It can only be done in the sea | It is a fast sprint for one length only | It needs a diving board to start
test: Which phrase means to use the sidestroke? | run sidestroke | sidestroke the ball | sidestroke off the wall | *do the sidestroke
exam: Why does a lifesaver choose sidestroke to rescue a tired swimmer? | It keeps the face out of the water and saves energy while towing | *It keeps the face out of the water and saves energy while towing someone | It makes the swimmer float like a log with no effort | It is the fastest racing stroke in the pool
